Package: kind-miner
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: d-Martian <d-Martian@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: apt-transport-tor, libc6, libgl1, libx11-6, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxinerama1, libxrandr2, libxxf86vm1
Recommends: tor
Conflicts: kind-minerd
Replaces: kind-minerd
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/d-Martian/Kind-Miner
Description: Monero miner that uses only the CPU you aren't using
 kind-miner mines Monero on P2Pool over Tor, in the background of a desktop
 you use, and steps aside the moment you need the machine. It has a window
 and a tray icon, and is set up from the window on first run.
 .
 The package ships xmrig, p2pool and Tor, and upgrades itself weekly from
 its own repository over Tor. It cannot be installed beside kind-minerd,
 the service for machines with no screen: two miners on one machine would
 compete for the same CPU.
